## 2. Time conventions

- **Demand.** Each value is the mean demand over the hour that **ends** at the timestamp, in UTC. The first hour of the series is stamped {{ c['demand_window'].metrics.first_utc|utc }}: midnight to 1 a.m. Eastern Standard Time.
- **Weather.** The temperature at a UTC hour is the observation made at that instant; it is requested from ECCC in UTC. Without an explicit time zone the service returns rows with no values, so the download refuses any response whose header is not in UTC.
- **Days.** For daily aggregates, an hour belongs to the day (Eastern Standard Time, UTC−5) in which it **starts**.
- **Daylight saving.** Everything is kept in UTC, where each hour exists once. {% if dm.missing_record_hours == 0 %}Outside the cases in sections 3.1 and 3.2, no UTC hour is absent from the export (blank values are in section 3.3): the spring change leaves no gap in it.{% else %}Outside the cases in sections 3.1 and 3.2, {{ dm.missing_record_hours }} UTC hours are absent from the export (section 3.3).{% endif +%}

