### Gates

A gate that fails stops the chain: no canonical data is written and the command exits with an error. Each one has a test that injects the fault it must catch.

| Check | Result | Measure | Threshold |
|---|---|---|---|
| Expected window, no record outside it | {{ c['demand_window'].passed|verdict }} | {{ c['demand_window'].metrics.outside }} outside | 0 |
| Every duplicate matches a known shape | {{ c['demand_duplicates_resolved'].passed|verdict }} | {{ c['demand_duplicates_resolved'].metrics.unresolved }} unresolved | 0 |
| Values within loose physical bounds ({{ c['demand_window'].metrics.first_utc[:4] }}–{{ c['demand_window'].metrics.last_utc[:4] }}) | {{ c['demand_bounds'].passed|verdict }} | {{ c['demand_bounds'].metrics.min_mw|num }} to {{ c['demand_bounds'].metrics.max_mw|num }} MW | {{ c['demand_bounds'].metrics.low_mw|num }} to {{ c['demand_bounds'].metrics.high_mw|num }} MW |
| Share of usable hours | {{ c['demand_coverage'].passed|verdict }} | {{ c['demand_coverage'].metrics.usable_share|pct(2) }} | ≥ {{ c['demand_coverage'].metrics.threshold|pct(0) }} |

### 3.1 Clocks going back: masked hours

{% if c['demand_dst'].metrics.events == 0 %}
No night of clocks going back leaves an anomaly in the window.
{% else %}
On the night clocks go back, local 1 a.m. happens twice. In the data, both values arrive under the UTC stamp of the second one, and the UTC hour before is missing. Nothing says which came first.

To judge whether continuity could order them, we compare the length of the path previous hour → first → second → next hour in both orders. When both orders give almost the same path, a guess would be arbitrary. Both hours are therefore masked every time, the same way.

| Night (repeated local hour) | Missing UTC hour | Values received (MW) | Path, better order (MW) | Path, other order (MW) | Margin (MW) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for e in c['demand_dst'].evidence %}
| {{ e.local_wall_clock[:16] }} | {{ e.missing_utc|utc }} | {{ e.values_mw[0]|num(2) }}; {{ e.values_mw[1]|num(2) }} | {{ e.continuity_cost_mw[0]|num }} | {{ e.continuity_cost_mw[1]|num }} | {{ e.continuity_margin_mw|num }} |
{% endfor %}

The margin ranges from {{ c['demand_dst'].metrics.min_margin_mw|num }} to {{ c['demand_dst'].metrics.max_margin_mw|num }} MW. A rule that ordered some nights and not others would be fragile.
{% endif %}

### 3.2 Misplaced record: repair with evidence

{% for e in c['demand_misplaced'].evidence %}
The timestamp {{ e.duplicated_utc|utc }} carries two values while {{ e.moved_to_utc|utc }} has none. The value {{ e.moved_mw|num(2) }} MW fits naturally between the neighbours of {{ e.moved_to_utc|utc }}, and {{ e.kept_mw|num(2) }} MW between those of {{ e.duplicated_utc|utc }}. The total path is {{ e.cost_mw|num }} MW in this assignment against {{ e.swapped_cost_mw|num }} MW the other way round: a ratio of {{ e.cost_ratio|num(1) }}. The rule needs a ratio of at least {{ c['demand_misplaced'].metrics.min_ratio|num(1) }} to move a value; otherwise nothing moves and the gate fails. The value is therefore moved, and the hour is labelled "repaired" in the canonical series.
{% else %}
